From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brian Ling <brianling16@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 07 Nov 2026 21:18:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] net/mlx5: derive WQ size capability in legacy verbs mode

Without DevX, HCA attributes are not queried and log_max_wq_sz stays
zero. Descriptor adjustment then clamps the requested RX/TX rings to
one entry, and receive queue creation fails. RX queue validation also
uses this capability, so changing descriptor reporting alone is not
sufficient.

Derive a conservative power-of-two limit from the verbs-reported
max_qp_wr when DevX is unavailable. Leave the DevX capability unchanged.

Verified with ConnectX-4 Lx firmware 14.18.2030 on Linux 5.15: the
Caladan DPDK IOKernel starts, TCP read tests pass, and its runtime
responds to ICMP over the physical experiment NIC.

---
 drivers/net/mlx5/linux/mlx5_os.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/mlx5/linux/mlx5_os.c b/drivers/net/mlx5/linux/mlx5_os.c
index 573e846ed2..e01cbd5697 100644
--- a/drivers/net/mlx5/linux/mlx5_os.c
+++ b/drivers/net/mlx5/linux/mlx5_os.c
@@ -175,6 +175,10 @@ mlx5_os_capabilities_prepare(struct mlx5_dev_ctx_shared *sh)
 	else
 		sh->dev_cap.sf = 1;
 	sh->dev_cap.max_qp_wr = attr_ex.orig_attr.max_qp_wr;
+	/* DevX HCA attributes are not populated in legacy Verbs mode. */
+	if (!cdev->config.devx && sh->dev_cap.max_qp_wr > 0)
+		hca_attr->log_max_wq_sz =
+			rte_fls_u32(sh->dev_cap.max_qp_wr) - 1;
 	sh->dev_cap.max_sge = attr_ex.orig_attr.max_sge;
 	sh->dev_cap.max_cq = attr_ex.orig_attr.max_cq;
 	sh->dev_cap.max_qp = attr_ex.orig_attr.max_qp;
